  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e1bd7ffe4606ce749a81aac1c495eb14, type: 3}
  m_Name: Note_SignalDiscovery1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: Responses to the Signal
  key: 13
  topic: 1
  boardContentText: 'Light patterns produced consistent responses


    The signal
    appeared to be interpreted'
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: 'Test 1, pattern A, 47 repetitions. Response in 44 cases. Time delay
    between transmission and reaction: constant, average 14 minutes.


    Test 2,
    pattern B, 31 repetitions. Response in 29 cases. Change in fog density correlated
    with amplitude.


    Test 3, pattern C, control noise. No response.


    CONCLUSION

    The
    signal is not received by the environment at random. Something distinguishes
    it from noise and reacts selectively according to the input pattern.


    HYPOTHESIS

    What
    interprets the signal does not merely understand it. Some of the as yet unclassified
    environmental anomalies may be a response... a pattern in return. We assume the
    other side is also transmitting.


    We recommend preparing equipment capable
    of reception.

'
  paperSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cea3c49c6ad23de4286197f5004fc48e, type: 3}
